{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515277-a-vampire-drawing-the-second-breath","id":1515277,"title":"A Vampire drawing the Second Breath","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-16T11:57:03-07:00","id":1515277,"title":"A Vampire drawing the Second Breath","content":"Although some books claim it to be rare, vampires can become wraiths; with this in mind, do you think somebody of requisite lineage be embraced, die, become a guest of Honour for the Yama Kings, and then claw their way back into a corpse (not their own, naturally). Moreover, I wonder what the reaction would be from everybody else (Possibly &quot;not <i>you </i>again!&quot;\u200b Surprise! Your new student is one of the (Chinese) della Passaglia or Wu Zao, back from &quot;Final&quot; Death to be a pain in the ass all over again )<br /> <br /> I don't mix the two games myself, but the concept has always made me wonder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-16-2023, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T14:07:25-07:00","id":1515299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515277-a-vampire-drawing-the-second-breath#post1515277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although some books claim it to be rare, vampires can become wraiths; with this in mind, do you think somebody of requisite lineage be embraced, die, become a guest of Honour for the Yama Kings, and then claw their way back into a corpse (not their own, naturally). Moreover, I wonder what the reaction would be from everybody else (Possibly &quot;not <i>you </i>again!&quot;\u200b Surprise! Your new student is one of the della Passaglia or Wu Zao, back from &quot;Final&quot; Death to be a pain in the ass all over again )<br /> <br /> I don't mix the two games myself, but the concept has always made me wonder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Complicated even if you do mix both games, i'd say.<br /> <br /> A della Passaglia and other &quot;stranger in a strange land&quot; individuals simply do not have the cultural background/paradigm to fit under the purview of the cosmology the Yomi Worlds are part of in the first place, they simply do not fall into the incarnation cycle from which the souls that would become Wan Kuei get snatched into the thousand hells.<br /> <br /> Only possible exception would be individual kindred that somehow attracted the personal attention of one Yama Kings, specially if that involves dealings with entities from Yomi and other stuff that would resonate with the ways of Akuma. People like Oliver Thrace perhaps. These kindred managed to make themselves special enough for at least one of the Yama Kings to have preparations set for when they are finally destroyed. What in itself is a problem, because having gained <i>the personal notice of a Yama King</i> means a degree of interest much greater in <b>keeping their souls there</b> than the average person who escaped the throngs of the Thousand Hells unoticed to draw the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Second_Breath_(KOTE)\" target=\"_blank\">Second Breath</a>.<br /> <br /> Plus, they would simply rise as as <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Chih-mei\" target=\"_blank\">Chih-meh</a>, meaning they would have to be captured, tamed and taught in the ways of Dharma and the disciplines of the Wan-Kuei, from zero. Not like the disciplines from its existence as kindred will be backwards compatible. Maybe such a &quot;kindred turned Wan Kuei&quot; might count on past infernalist knowledge to become a self-taught Akuma or Devil Tiger - and maybe get a &quot;discipline buffer&quot; of sorts from this wellspring of occult lore depending on ST leniency.<br /> <br /> So, as you can see, there are a lots of &quot;maybes&quot; and &quot;ifs&quot; involved in every step of this road to hell and back for one to make it work. Kindred westerners who &quot;just are there&quot; and develop little to no interaction with the Yama Kings - and would be the largest majority of such western intruders might be said, members of della Passaglia's branch of the Giovanni included since necromancers in general are connected to either corpse-rising or the inhabitants of the Yin World, that happens to be a different spirit realm - would be in the &quot;not compatible&quot; to &quot;less than a blip&quot; camp.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now individuals who do come southeast asian cultural paradigms and just happen to get embraced - i dare say that is a place where things get considerably more complicated, since some might consider their condition to sort of put them &quot;outside the wheel&quot; and yet a part of the world. That can definitely led into some very complex to define and label places <b>indeed</b>. The kind of heavy metaphysical discussion that i dare say most of KotE original writers would cry tears of blood and pay lots of hard cash <b>not</b> to get dragged into. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But to overly simplify things, let's say that where a chinese Wu Zao, vietnamese Nagaraja or indian Tzimisce or Malkavian ends up in the afterlife might depend strongly on how well they stood up for whatever Path/Road they took in their unlife, with some room for debate depending on how the Path morals fit with cultural mores of their breathing years.<br /> <br /> Much, much lower chances of ending up as one of the inhabitants of the Yomi World than the previous anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-16-2023, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T14:31:55-07:00","id":1515304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515277-a-vampire-drawing-the-second-breath?p=1515299#post1515299\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A della Passaglia and other &quot;stranger in a strange land&quot; individuals simply do not have the cultural background/paradigm to fit under the purview of the cosmology the Yomi Worlds are part of in the first place, they simply do not fall into the incarnation cycle from which the souls that would become Wan Kuei get snatched into the thousand hells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Debatable. The older, Western part of the clan are foreigners, but as time and the setting moved on they've become more local. They have married their way into influential Chinese families, and one of their canon family members, a ghoul named Kwei who was born and raised in Hong Kong, clearly identifies himself as being Asian vs the Giovanni &quot;Westerners&quot; who are his (whatever relation, uh, was it Martino or Antonio? is to him)'s relatives.<br /> Their Catholic background is likewise irrelevant, as the Dark Ages supplement offers a convert who has to struggle with their Faith after the Second Breath as a character concept.<br /> <br /> Like, the members of the family who have Asian ancestry, were raised with said Asian culture and incorporate it into their paradigm (parts of tradition Chinese religion like ancestor worship being the big one) count, imo. They don't count any less than the Asian-American Hungry Dead who are shaped by Western influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-16-2023, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T14:52:50-07:00","id":1515307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515277-a-vampire-drawing-the-second-breath?p=1515304#post1515304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Debatable. The older, Western part of the clan are foreigners, but as time and the setting moved on they've become more local. They have married their way into influential Chinese families, and one of their canon family members, a ghoul named Kwei who was born and raised in Hong Kong, clearly identifies himself as being Asian vs the Giovanni &quot;Westerners&quot; who are his (whatever relation, uh, was it Martino or Antonio? is to him)'s relatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well duh, everything related to KotE is debatable from the get-go - people are all too quick to forget that supernaturals are also prone to mythologizing things and that they believe the cosmology works in a certain way does not make it a factual truth. That's the whole starting problem when it comes to the matter of &quot;who becomes one of the Wan Kuei&quot; in the first place. The writers of KotE were not anywhere near as versed in the cultures they felt like adressing as they imagined themselves to be and it tells.<br /> <br /> On the matter of how really immersed or not are della Passaglias in chinese society and cultures, honestly i'd have to look into whatever books you are using as reference.<br /> (And take with several grains of salt any that are V5, because context matters and while the V5 writers are overall well-meaning much of the implementation of lore leaves a lot to be desired)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515277-a-vampire-drawing-the-second-breath?p=1515304#post1515304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their Catholic background is likewise irrelevant, as the Dark Ages supplement offers a convert who has to struggle with their Faith after the Second Breath as a character concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>That can be complex - cultural background/paradigm can go beyond just an individual's personal beliefs/faith, as shown by Richard Gere and any Hollywood star converted to Buddhism. As an aside, what Dark Ages supplement are you speaking of? I would like to take a look for reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T15:07:47-07:00","id":1515311,"title":"","content":"And there goes the stupid spam philter swallowing people's messages because of a quick edit again. Wonderful. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-16T23:43:50-07:00","id":1515331,"title":"","content":"I would say IF that would happen, the members of the <b>Raktasadhu of India </b>are prime candidates<br /> Daitya, Danava, Nagaraja, Eastern Ravnos, the Wu Zao or even Kartarirya's Tzimsice brood... or even soem lurking Baali<br /> India more or less a &quot;contested teritory&quot; anyway; the Infinite Thunders Court of southern India and the Golden Court of eastern India are an everpresent danger/enemy there and the Yama King Ravana I guess would be especially delighted to drag some Ravnos soul in to her ruined Hell, but Tou Mu Yama Queen of the Hell of Being Skinned Alive, who presiding over the hoarders and abusers of power I guess either would be an ally - since she hates the Kuei-Jin - or an eager foe, who by divine mandate would try to snach a few souls. After all, if anyone is the hoarder and abuser of power, then that is a vampire<br /> Wu Hua in the Pit of Salt and Iron, who presiding over the souls of traitors, Hine-Nui-Te-Po, who presiding over the souls of those who committed suicide, and Dou Tingzhang, the Mutilator of the Unfaithful probably would be interested too, while Malaveyovo, who presiding over cannibals and hungry Same-Bito (proving not even shapeshifters are out of the reach of a Yama King) would be delighted to have a few Nagaraja soul around and Ku of the Thousand Tears, who rules from Feng-tu and is the patron of the Wu-Keng wuld be especially interested to aquire some Baali...<br /> And the Divine Mandate from the August Personage of Jade and the Celestial Bureaucracy actually makes them possible - in the right circumstances - to calim a soul<br /> If anything the Great Leap Outward proved this; bbservations in San Francisco show that the Kuei-jin carry the reach of the Yomi World with them. This allows the Yama Kings to access resources that they do not have within their traditional domains.<br /> Where they go, Yomi goes too... (and given the cold but very polite diplomatic realtionship, sending of slaves, gifts and emissaries back and forth between the Maeljin of Malfeas and the Yama Kings of Yomi could be a horrifying story hook)<br /> The K\u00e0nbuji\u00e0n from Kindred of the East Companion and San Francisco by Night are Kuei-jin that have taken the Second Breath <i>outside</i> the Middle Kingdom and somehow managed to transcend their chih-mei phase out of sheer force of will... the reverse technically could happen if the circumstances are &quot;right&quot;, from purely &quot;celestial law of point of view&quot;, India is part of the Middle Kingdom, so a claimed Daitya, Danava, Nagaraja, Eastern Ravnos, the Wu Zao, Kartarirya's get or Baali - or really any Cainite who is &quot;not a westener (why am I feeling I'm dancing on a mine field littered with egg shels, blindfolded and bare footed...? ) is a prime candidate to be claimed by Yomi and probably escape.<br /> <br /> But if you want further, we have the Giovanni family. the Li Weng - Chinese geomancers<br /> This especially could be interesting since Mikaboshi himself was originally a Japanese scholar and fang shih who was invited by the Chinese court to be an advisor who himself used geomancy, and turned to infernalism. He created many architectural configurations to develop and focus corrupted chi through the Yin world to fuel his magics, but was eventually found out, forcing him to flee into the spirit worlds permanently and eventually became a Yama King and of course Ravana is widely accepted once were Zapatahsura's children, a Ravnos prior his ascension...\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T04:48:40-07:00","id":1515344,"title":"","content":"An intriguing thought occurred to me years ago: that Yama Kings might occasionally send particularly awful souls back to the Middle Kingdom for the express purpose of defiling it. This could be one of those situations where it might make sense for your game.<br /> <br /> Once the Yama Kings have a soul, it stops spreading misery. Sure, every soul is a battery of Demon Chi, in its own twisted version of the Matrix, but a good proselytiser is worth hundreds of souls as opposed to one.<br /> <br /> If you were a Yama King, allowing certain particularly monstrous beings to &quot;escape&quot; and return to the world to cause more suffering would be a smart move. You just have to balance the risk against losing an eternity of Demon Chi from one being against the potential gains of many more beings coming to you in time.<br /> <br /> So even if the metaphysics seem improbable, you always have the &quot;deus ex machina&quot; of meddling Yama Kings to let this happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-17T04:55:16-07:00","id":1515346,"title":"","content":"When I manage to find a team who want to play KotE I sometimes to use this &quot;possibility&quot;, giving the game a bit Changeling: the Lost feeling<br /> The atmosphere <i>uncertanity </i>and dread<br /> Are they<i> really</i> escaped...? Or the Yama Kings let them go to be their unwitting agents and their deeds on the long run serves Yomi... or not? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T02:59:35-07:00","id":1515639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As an aside, what Dark Ages supplement are you speaking of? I would like to take a look for reference. </div> </div> </div>Turned out to be Victorian, not Dark Ages. Didn't find the exact part, but here's a part about religion amongst the Gaki in <i>Sunset Empires</i> that says pretty much the same thing;<br /> &quot;Before the Edo Period, Japan held about 300,000 Roman Catholics, many of whom died in the Shogunate's purge. <i>A few of these took the Second Breath.</i>&quot; They're not liked or trusted, and they themselves are torn between loyalty to their fellow undead and to the Church.<br /> <br /> Not to mention regions like Bangladesh, Malaysia and Indonesia which are a Muslim majority but still fall under the influence of the &quot;Middle Kingdom&quot; as far as I recall. I don't remember what the setting had to say on the matter, but in practice, either the Golden Courts' newest members are muslim penanggalan, or else their potential numbers have dropped with the Abrahamic 72% of the population now being off the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-20-2023, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-20T16:32:23-07:00","id":1515704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1515277-a-vampire-drawing-the-second-breath?p=1515639#post1515639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Turned out to be Victorian, not Dark Ages. Didn't find the exact part, but here's a part about religion amongst the Gaki in <i>Sunset Empires</i> that says pretty much the same thing;<br /> &quot;Before the Edo Period, Japan held about 300,000 Roman Catholics, many of whom died in the Shogunate's purge. <i>A few of these took the Second Breath.</i>&quot; They're not liked or trusted, and they themselves are torn between loyalty to their fellow undead and to the Church.<br /> <br /> Not to mention regions like Bangladesh, Malaysia and Indonesia which are a Muslim majority but still fall under the influence of the &quot;Middle Kingdom&quot; as far as I recall. I don't remember what the setting had to say on the matter, but in practice, either the Golden Courts' newest members are muslim penanggalan, or else their potential numbers have dropped with the Abrahamic 72% of the population now being off the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that dovetails quite well into the &quot;myths and their own claims notwithstanding, the Wan Kuei themselves have little to no idea of the actual process behind how the whole thing really works at all&quot; point i brought up previously - IF they are correct about how it relates to the Yama Kings and the spiritual enviroment, cultural value set, paradigm they are an element of, a kindred that turns wraith actually drawing is <b>quite </b>improbable, <b>but </b>perhapspossible in certain <i><b>very </b></i>particular circunstances.<br /> <br /> Now, if one nitpicks as you do at the many doubts, inconsistencies and issues that enter the equation when factors of geography, religion and regional culture &amp; history are brought into the mix - <b>and</b> yes, i agree there are a hefty bunch of them, KotE's original writing team didn't give their little pet nowhere near as much thought or attention to research as they should - or outright states they are utterly incorrect, well you have just entered the undiscovered country, no points of reference or anything close to a halfway passable criteria to argue from beside &quot;i want it to be so as a ST&quot;.<br /> <br /> So the real issue is more like &quot;how to make sense of it in a way that entertains my group of players or whoever is reading this, instead of causing people to throw their hands, cry shenanigans/b#ll$#it! and starting arguing with me?&quot;, in the end i dare say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}